  "problem": "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ \\frac{{v}_{1}}{\u2016{v}_{1}\u2016} & \\frac{{v}_{2}}{\u2016{v}_{2}\u2016} & \\frac{{v}_{3}}{\u2016{v}_{3}\u2016} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above, where ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is an orthogonal set of vectors. You're given that $\u2016{v}_{1}\u2016=1,$ $\u2016{v}_{2}\u2016=3,$ $\u2016{v}_{3}\u2016=2,$ and that the system of equations below describes the relationship between the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$ \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}={a}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2}={a}_{2}-3{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{3}={a}_{3}-{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{12}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{23}?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we normalize the vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{\u2016{v}_{1}\u2016}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{1}\\,\u27f9\\,{v}_{1}={q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{\u2016{v}_{2}\u2016}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{3}\\,\u27f9\\,{v}_{2}=3{q}_{2} \\\\ {q}_{3} & =\\frac{{v}_{3}}{\u2016{v}_{3}\u2016}=\\frac{{v}_{3}}{2}\\,\u27f9\\,{v}_{3}=2{q}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the set ${{q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}}$ will be both orthogonal and normalized.\n\nNext, let's rewrite the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ as a linear combination of the vectors ${q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}={a}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2}={a}_{2}-3{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{3}={a}_{3}-{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}={v}_{1}={q}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}=3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=3{q}_{1}+3{q}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{3}={v}_{1}+2{v}_{2}+{v}_{3}={q}_{1}+6{q}_{2}+2{q}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final system can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{r}_{12}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{23}=3+3+6=12.\n$$",
